# Line-ending policy.
#
# Everything in this repository ultimately runs inside Linux containers, so the
# committed form is LF and git must not rewrite it on checkout.
#
# This is not cosmetic. `infra/docker/entrypoint_mcp.sh` is the ENTRYPOINT of all
# four MCP containers. Checked out with CRLF, its shebang becomes `#!/usr/bin/env sh\r`
# and the kernel looks for an interpreter literally named "sh\r" — every MCP container
# fails to start. `scripts/security/compile_requirements.sh` fails the same way, on
# `set -euo pipefail\r`.
#
# Note that CI cannot catch this class of bug: a Linux runner checks out LF whatever
# the repository says. It only appears when building from a Windows or macOS clone,
# which is precisely why it belongs in a file rather than in someone's local config.

# Default: let git detect text files, and keep LF in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Executables interpreted by a shell — the shebang must not carry a CR.
*.sh            text eol=lf
entrypoint*     text eol=lf

# Container and orchestration definitions, read by Linux tooling.
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.ini           text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.mako          text eol=lf

# Never touched by the newline filter.
*.pdf           binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pem           binary
*.key           binary
